[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Input shape axes:** the sole input is one 32-bit `float` passed by value. The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m code does not inspect its value — it `memcpy`s the object representation and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m formats each of the 4 bytes with `%02x`. So the shape axes that the *observable
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m output* actually distinguishes are:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **Per-byte value class** — which drives `%02x`: bytes `0x00`, `0x01..0x0f`
